<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- TODO Four capabilities belong here and none can be added yet: a Personal Team cannot sign
	     them, so Xcode does not offer them under Signing & Capabilities, and writing the key by
	     hand only breaks the build. All wait on the paid Apple Developer Program.

	       · com.apple.developer.devicecheck.appattest-environment (production) — App Check's
	         App Attest in release builds. Without it their requests carry no valid token.

	       · aps-environment (development) — without it there is no FCM on iOS.
	       · com.apple.developer.applesignin — without it the Apple button on the sign-in screen
	         fails every time.
	       · com.apple.developer.associated-domains = applinks:turnia.club (the host in
	         InvitationLinkConfig) — without it an invitation link opens the web page instead of
	         the app. The page's own button still opens the app through its custom scheme, and the
	         site already serves the apple-app-site-association file this needs (firebase/hosting).

	     Adding the entitlement is the last step of each, not the only one. See
	     "Pending: the paid Apple Developer Program" in CLAUDE.md. -->
</dict>
</plist>
